======================================================================
Interactive usage
======================================================================

To start an interactive shell locally or on an SSH host using the
remote-ssh environment:

  @SHELL_COMMAND@

The current directory is preserved. Use exit to return to the calling shell.
The equivalent manual Bash launch is also available as a fallback:

  @INTERACTIVE_COMMAND@

remote-ssh's shell environment is Bash-first. Do not source shell/rc.sh from
Zsh; use the shell command or manual Bash launch shown above.


Installation exposes only the management CLI and selected tool binaries in
INSTALL_BIN_DIR. Prompt, aliases and checkout helpers activate only in this
explicit Bash session. Startup files and the default shell are not changed.

The management link points to this checkout. Moving or deleting the checkout
can break it; updating this checkout updates the command. Reinstalls reuse only
the direct canonical link. Conflicting entries, including other checkouts or
relative/chained equivalent links, are preserved: inspect and move or remove
one deliberately, or choose another INSTALL_BIN_DIR.

Uninstall and prune retain the management link and checkout. For full manual
removal, inspect the link and remove it only if it still points to the checkout
being removed. Configure INSTALL_BIN_DIR in PATH for ordinary/new terminals;
an earlier PATH entry may shadow the command. The installer edits no profiles.
